# M4.29.2 Agentmode protected-home SSH access failure

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

The second authorized start produced external state immediately, but its state
was fail-closed:

- `CONTROL_REMOTE_CHECK_FAILED`
- `DOCS_SYNC_FAILED`
- remote SHA `-`

The 60-second installation gate therefore stopped Agentmode, Integrity and
Monitor. All eight installed artifact hashes matched the committed manifest.

## Evidence and cause

As `chatops` outside the unit, the exact `git ls-remote` probe against
`refs/heads/control-main` succeeded and returned
`2c17ae00d9c9b6e057ba36a1766166f7f5549d4c`. The repositories use SSH aliases
and deploy keys under `/home/chatops/.ssh`.

The Agentmode unit specified `ProtectHome=yes`, which makes the entire home
tree inaccessible inside the service namespace. Both the read-only Control
remote probe and the deliberately retained Docs synchronization consequently
lost access to their SSH configuration and keys.

## Impact

- Control HEAD/tree/refs/tracked state: unchanged;
- Adult Candidate: inactive, dead, static, `NRestarts=0`, never started;
- Integrity and Monitor: not restarted after the failed gate;
- Agentmode: stopped by the error trap;
- provider/token/media/payment/publishing paths: untouched.

## Remediation and rollback

Use `ProtectHome=read-only` for Agentmode. This exposes the existing SSH
configuration and deploy keys read-only while denying all service writes to
home directories. Keep `ReadOnlyPaths=/opt/tu1nz_repos/control` unchanged.
Add a regression assertion for the exact sandbox value, rebind the unit hash in
the manifest, run the complete local suite, commit, push and wait for green CI
before reinstalling that unit.

If the corrected start does not reach a valid observation, stop all three
maintenance services and leave them stopped. Restore old bytes only from the
root-private recovery archive and only while services are stopped; never
automatically restart the archived unsafe Agentmode.
